                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "random question:\n\n`num-chassis-smp` meson option defines this, right?\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-state-manager/+/88928/5\n\nCan we hardcode it here as `12` or do we need to derive it from the meson option."
                },
                {
                    "file": "obmcutil",
                    "line": 517,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, I couldn't come up with an easy solution to get the meson.option into this file. I could rename it to obmcutil.in (template file) and then do a @NUM_CHASSIS_SMP@ for the 12, but then you can't just copy the obmcutil onto a system and start using it. So....not sure the added complexity is worth it for a verbose debug option in here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "obmcutil",
                    "line": 517,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "makes sense, maybe not worth it for verbose debug options \ud83d\udc4d"
                }
            ],
